Z||000009||Fiasco||05-11-2000||05:02 PM||||You can find way more info. on trouble codes here on the forum and on other sites such as FOCOA's and V8 Archies. Here is one with a fairly detailed explanation of testing for codes: <A HREF="http://argo.acronet.net/~abarthel/repair.html" TARGET=_blank>http://argo.acronet.net/~abarthel/repair.html</A> <BR>Don't get me wrong, though, you should have a manual, too.||||reg||4
Z||000010||theogre||05-11-2000||06:37 PM||||Vacuum leaks and incorrect base timing will cause this more often than anything else.<P>DO NOT mess with the Idle stop screw. The only time this should be an issue is when replacing the TBI unit.||||reg||1
